homelab-keepalived (0.1.3) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Release v0.1.3

 -- Gardner <gardner@homelab>  Sun, 25 Oct 2026 22:54:08 -0500

homelab-keepalived (0.1.3) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Notify-managed public VIPs via a new `dhcp_vips:` list in vrrp.yml. Each
    entry floats a public IP on a macvlan carrying a SPECIFIC reservation MAC
    and takes its address via DHCP -- NOT a keepalived virtual_ipaddress,
    which would present the host NIC's MAC or a VRRP 00:00:5e:00:01:xx vMAC
    that the upstream pfSense/CARP rejects. New homelab-keepalived-notify
    hook (wired via notify_master/backup/fault) builds/tears the macvlan and
    runs dhclient; new homelab-keepalived-dhclient-script applies ONLY the
    leased address (no default route -> no egress hijack, no resolv.conf
    rewrite). mode: dhcp (pure) | static+dhcp (static for instant failover
    with DHCP alongside to re-register the reservation MAC).
  * apply now writes /etc/homelab/keepalived/dhcp-vips.conf (the notify spec,
    regenerated every run so it never drifts) and opens DHCP (UDP 67/68) in
    the no-flush nft drop-in when dhcp_vips are present. keepalived-managed
    `vips:` and notify-managed `dhcp_vips:` can coexist in the one instance.
  * Ship /etc/sysctl.d/60-homelab-keepalived-arp.conf (arp_ignore=1,
    arp_announce=2) so multi-homed VIP ARP hygiene is packaged, not
    hand-placed; postinst loads it. Depends: iproute2, isc-dhcp-client,
    iputils-arping. postrm purge tears down leftover macvlans + DHCP rules.

 -- Gardner <gardner@homelab>  Sat, 25 Oct 2026 20:05:00 -0500

homelab-keepalived (0.1.2) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Release v0.1.2

 -- Gardner <gardner@homelab>  Sun, 25 Oct 2026 16:13:23 -0500

homelab-keepalived (0.1.2) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Float multiple VIPs, each on its own interface, via a new `vips:` list
    in vrrp.yml (one public IP per interface; all float together in the one
    VRRP instance so a single node owns them). Original single `vip:`/
    `vip_interface:` form still accepted. Optional `default_route_interface`
    pins the master-only default route (else the first vip's interface).
    apply-script paths are env-overridable for testing; added t/apply.t.

 -- Gardner <gardner@homelab>  Sun, 25 Oct 2026 16:13:15 -0500

